{"title":"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d41c4438c8dfad08aa1f927b5852d79dc1ea5195.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e80c6b6a84ad4015ea436a915435d69edbdd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5429dc4aa7ba1f3b20be4599a34c4220cc79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/e/a0e5885f9fdc85e2bb9646b7f924384112b81f3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd5522d5f3ee8be2aac7d8d04ba78a64a4de17db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 13 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 17 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 19 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The average of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> numbers would be the sum of the numbers divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Applying this, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers and that the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243ca0eb22942ec4e4da5cc51334813f005fc1ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - 3 + n - 1 + n + 1 + n + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"237\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>We see that the constant terms cancel out and we are left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b417a127620d5b467fe7a48ad5f7d843e5c390b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>The average can then be represented with the following equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bedf6aedddcdce32754e629b528e2dbeb92297aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4n}{4} = 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a057c3d4a65657effee625f4382094b38df9d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because all of the constant terms are mirrored with sign around <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/6/366394b3d4e7671efa756b8a5052317097534a01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1 + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/9/a89eed108c47772074803f9e482918ff2768ffa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3 + 3 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />), we see that the average must also be equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> without doing any other calculation.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/0/4a057c3d4a65657effee625f4382094b38df9d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed {\\textbf {(C) } 17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley\">2025 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <